## Logging Rules (Non-Negotiable)

### General
- Services MUST NOT contain any logging statements.
- Repositories MUST NOT contain logging statements.
- UI components and hooks MUST NOT log business events.


### Service Logging
- All service entry, exit, and error logging MUST be applied via container-level logger proxies.
- `loggerProxy` MUST be used only in `src/container.ts`.
- Cursor MUST reuse the existing `loggerProxy` and MUST NOT introduce new logging patterns.

### Central Logger
- All logging MUST go through the centralized logger (`logger.ts`).
- Logging destinations (local file, remote/Sentry, disabled) MUST be controlled centrally in `logger.ts`.
- Cursor MUST NOT introduce direct file logging or Sentry calls outside the logger.

### Local File Logging
- Local file logging is allowed ONLY via:
  `logger.ts → localFileLogger.ts → src/platform/fileSystem.ts`
- Expo FileSystem APIs MUST ONLY be used inside `src/platform/fileSystem.ts`.
- All other layers MUST use the platform fileSystem abstraction.

### Log Export
- Log export MUST be triggered only by explicit user action (e.g., Settings screen).
- Cursor MUST NOT introduce automatic or background log uploads.
- Log export MUST use `exportLogsForSupport`.
- Log export MUST include device and app metadata using `getDeviceAndAppInfo`.
- Metadata collection MUST NOT include user identifiers or PII.
- Log export MUST NOT read database files directly.
- Log export MUST use the platform fileSystem abstraction only.

### Data Safety
- Sensitive fields MUST NEVER appear in logs.
- All logged payloads MUST respect allowlists and masking rules.
